    "body": "> I agree that this would be a step in the right direction. [w3c/navigation-timing#160 (comment)](https://github.com/w3c/navigation-timing/issues/160#issuecomment-951801611) (by you!) has notes on potentially making it even better. (I say potentially, as perhaps WebKit already uses the start time of the latest fetch.)\r\n\r\nYea, that would be better IMO but more \"breaking\" in case of a navigation that starts with a cross-origin redirect.\r\n\r\n",
